Body:
It seems the latest version already supports switching. We can edit `~/.config/opencode/tui.json`

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/tui.json",
  "keybinds": {
    "input_submit": "ctrl+return,ctrl+s",
    "input_newline": "return,shift+return,alt+return,ctrl+j"
  }
}
```

In Windows Terminal, configure `settings.json` to enable `ctrl+enter` send `ctrl+enter` instead of `ctrl+j`

```json
{
    "actions": [
        {
            "command": {
                "action": "sendInput",
                "input": "\u001b[13;5u"
            },
            "id": "User.CtrlEnterCSIu"
        }
    ],
    "keybindings": [
        { "keys": "ctrl+enter", "id": "User.CtrlEnterCSIu" }
    ]
}
```

Tested successfully with `VERTEX_LOCATION=eu`
```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "enabled_providers": [
    "google-vertex-anthropic"
  ],
  "provider": {
    "google-vertex-anthropic": {
      "whitelist": [
        "claude-opus-4-7@default"
      ]
    },
  }
}
```

Before the patch lands, overwriting `baseURL` is a possible workaround:
```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "enabled_providers": [
    "google-vertex-anthropic"
  ],
  "provider": {
    "google-vertex-anthropic": {
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://aiplatform.eu.rep.googleapis.com/v1/projects/YOUR-PROJECT-HERE/locations/eu/publishers/anthropic/models/"
      },
      "whitelist": [
        "claude-opus-4-7@default"
      ]
    },
  }
}
```

